    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen012.png",
    "sha256": "c7cd7b83c3b94b0ba0bd4abf8c2d7726c7a7dcda49005b7983e34d4f08c1211c",
    "k": 11,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Now, listen to the mini-lecture.",
    "zh": "现在请听短讲。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "listen"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen013.png",
    "sha256": "a4a228772b86921305d7c5e729560c1c0966b02780953e56abb05b2bdb3364bd",
    "k": 12,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "When it is over, you will be given three minutes to check your work.",
    "zh": "短讲结束后，你将有三分钟检查作答。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "check"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen014.png",
    "sha256": "e5a35eaf91c7a57244876ce9d2f87263b03421a74c3b3d7ca07cd43573c66c57",
    "k": 13,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": "transition",
    "en": "Body language and mind.",
    "zh": "肢体语言与心智。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mind"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen015.png",
    "sha256": "eab0c5583154b32900c7f98e71da2cf65a21170d1a3c607d7abdd2a94f5e70ce",
    "k": 14,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Good morning everyone.",
    "zh": "大家早上好。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "good morning"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen016.png",
    "sha256": "e4a52dc08dc521729ef880d037d60e87ab1926fcde5692157fcd9d98f3bf2149",
    "k": 15,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "In today’s lecture, I’d like to focus on how our body language reveals who we are.",
    "zh": "今天这堂课，我想重点谈谈肢体语言如何揭示我们是怎样的人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "reveal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen017.png",
    "sha256": "fbcc5939ca2f2f352b8a540ea7f664b27f68d94b2dca3d66ca796a88929f52e4",
    "k": 16,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We are really fascinated with body language and particularly interested in other people’s body language.",
    "zh": "我们对肢体语言十分着迷，尤其关注别人的肢体语言。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "fascinated"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen018.png",
    "sha256": "88aa52460ab10ef89ad88969e0edd3933fa77042a7840c50dc8a31babc545ea5",
    "k": 17,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You know, we are sometimes interested in an awkward interaction, or a smile, or a contemptuous glance, or maybe a very awkward wink or handshake.",
    "zh": "有时，一个尴尬的互动、一个微笑、一道轻蔑的目光，或是一个很不自然的眨眼、握手，都会引起我们的兴趣。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "contemptuous"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen019.png",
    "sha256": "aaa1b2464e1f868fdf02573b8e2f6e7bf5e93643c185edd13bb1820b1f3a3c99",
    "k": 18,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, what kind of body language am I talking about?",
    "zh": "那么，我要谈的是哪种肢体语言呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "body language"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen020.png",
    "sha256": "b3c63b3027e8a3aaec4b5e070f20eafe2a6230bb08c371622b0babfbfbddd298",
    "k": 19,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I am interested in power dynamics.",
    "zh": "我关注的是权力关系的变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "power dynamics"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen021.png",
    "sha256": "aa043fd76f3c192e2fb1293623c2cea84795ba684e4f5c4b30d172a27939e492",
    "k": 20,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That is the non-verbal expressions of power and dominance.",
    "zh": "也就是权力和支配地位的非语言表达。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "dominance"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen022.png",
    "sha256": "1a444ae3a58e018fe84a8ab8a1e8888090b630bcad84e51ec5c6ffc8b70de98d",
    "k": 21,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And what are nonverbal expressions of power and dominance?",
    "zh": "那么，权力和支配地位有哪些非语言表达呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "nonverbal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen023.png",
    "sha256": "e9a52a69e9aa2fd19baa09d4060fc22af90d0a2451b58e4fcd06b9fbe4c1978d",
    "k": 22,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Well, this is what they are: in the animal kingdom, non-verbal expressions of power and dominance are about expanding.",
    "zh": "是这样的：在动物世界里，权力和支配地位的非语言表达，表现为身体向外扩张。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "expand"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen024.png",
    "sha256": "2ae308eef9e952ead0818883e2875a67cba4e644aa29f9b9e3f3187606fba3f1",
    "k": 23,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, you make yourself big, you stretch out, you take up space and you are basically opening up.",
    "zh": "也就是说，你让自己显得高大，伸展身体，占据空间，基本上就是把身体打开。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stretch out"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen025.png",
    "sha256": "570598197981225cb7708e54809c074f2b1186adc03423d57ac850457ee3ecb8",
    "k": 24,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And, and humans do the same thing.",
    "zh": "人类也有同样的表现。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "human"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen026.png",
    "sha256": "483a71019d2e95b0348e2cdc9e16a4accf98a01dfd4ff46887ad34a6d1768906",
    "k": 25,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, they do this when they are feeling powerful in the moment.",
    "zh": "当人们在某一刻感觉自己有力量时，就会这样做。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "powerful"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen027.png",
    "sha256": "1ba64354f18303bc06f874abe294c9d0285f0085374a511bf1ab8feb334a7b34",
    "k": 26,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And this one is especially interesting because it really shows us how universal and old these expressions of power are.",
    "zh": "这种表现尤其有趣，因为它确实让我们看到，这些表达力量的动作有多么普遍，历史又有多么久远。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "universal"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen028.png",
    "sha256": "9257194b2dc8c32e18feb3fa6f5130e1a347c823635b254d1c1fbffcace51af3",
    "k": 27,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For example, when athletes cross the finish line and they’ve won, it doesn’t matter if they’ve never seen anyone do it.",
    "zh": "例如，运动员冲过终点、赢得比赛时，哪怕从没见过别人这么做，也一样会做出这种动作。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "finish line"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen029.png",
    "sha256": "c2f8619395b9369f1bddb38807316d95d9e001788547079a1ab50ebb37ac9bac",
    "k": 28,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They do this: so, the arms are up in a ‘V’ sign, the chin is slightly lifted.",
    "zh": "他们会这样：双臂向上举成V字，下巴微微抬起。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "chin"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen030.png",
    "sha256": "b6497af611a76eae503c7ff964159e6630601ea21dc3987e969d32ce0fdfc025",
    "k": 29,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "But what do we do when we feel powerless?",
    "zh": "可是，当我们感觉自己没有力量时，又会怎么做呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "powerless"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen031.png",
    "sha256": "c024e2db2d5e38c02eabfc61239cab8beedf8160b17acd1ed62908eab9871e52",
    "k": 30,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We do exactly the opposite.",
    "zh": "我们的做法恰好相反。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "opposite"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen032.png",
    "sha256": "f996722160d0d2b857d9fa3eaeeedba1c1f4821e15aed00839a9e1de69d11134",
    "k": 31,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We close up.",
    "zh": "我们会收拢身体。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "close up"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen033.png",
    "sha256": "5c8d62dcc208dc4d7023b7790249aa96913b157f994ab613601b1c61054b2e2e",
    "k": 32,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We make ourselves small.",
    "zh": "让自己显得更小。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "make oneself small"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen034.png",
    "sha256": "2107e37757d4281f2a8754e08a51e3ac252dcb163ce24ddc2629d882b42a409c",
    "k": 33,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We don’t want to bump into the person next to us.",
    "zh": "我们不想碰到旁边的人。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "bump into"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen035.png",
    "sha256": "147b983b05e3bc33babdbc6f7e5ba5b37a989b543c9f319922b9ba8d1e404b3b",
    "k": 34,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And this is what happens when you put together high and low power.",
    "zh": "当强势者和弱势者处在一起时，就会出现这样的情况。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "put together"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen036.png",
    "sha256": "dc337324bdf04cc6bf16fafac6b0881024a4e3b28cb8940753321e5121cf6872",
    "k": 35,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, what we tend to do when it comes to power is that we complement the other’s non-verbals.",
    "zh": "因此，在权力关系中，我们往往会用与对方互补的非语言动作来回应。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "complement"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen037.png",
    "sha256": "14d068554d4a2e53ac1f6e50404d807232bab2955c58b4b05dafd33b9b9a92c0",
    "k": 36,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What I mean is, if someone is being really powerful with us, we tend to make ourselves smaller.",
    "zh": "我的意思是，如果有人对我们表现得很强势，我们往往会让自己的身体缩得更小。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "tend to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen038.png",
    "sha256": "3c09bba96e457dfc2eaf0fefad34f2aac8228b735dd3704aedfa1a5c4cff716b",
    "k": 37,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We don’t mirror them.",
    "zh": "我们不会模仿对方的动作。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mirror"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen039.png",
    "sha256": "9f8c6c91a1fb6f56f46b721d4627fcf09f2058ca3604c86fb9b0a7d579e84dc5",
    "k": 38,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We do the opposite.",
    "zh": "我们会作出相反的反应。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "opposite"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen040.png",
    "sha256": "df3a56842a52515f56e0837ca15a7b2f65f8c962aac227b31d2fcf8a2efad7e7",
    "k": 39,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I am watching this behavior in the classroom and guess what I have noticed.",
    "zh": "我一直在课堂上观察这种行为，猜猜我发现了什么。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "behavior"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen041.png",
    "sha256": "4a8de375c8d307ddb64a932021e368b0c7a4e21a8368ec8ac31b880c503162ab",
    "k": 40,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I noticed that MBA students really exhibit the full range of power non-verbals.",
    "zh": "我注意到，MBA学生的表现几乎涵盖了从强势到弱势的全部非语言动作。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "exhibit"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen042.png",
    "sha256": "8dda9d096bcff07e4ebf4c0543bda17e6a8edbc041f80011c5d717ea881cbc38",
    "k": 41,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They get right into the middle of the room before class even starts like they really want to occupy space.",
    "zh": "有些学生在上课前就径直走到教室中央，好像非常想占据空间。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "occupy"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen043.png",
    "sha256": "8144fdc17e4532546cc15986af506b98dfc0dadaf40066119e54f938a6fa7cec",
    "k": 42,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "When they sit down, they are sort of spread out.",
    "zh": "坐下时，他们的身体也舒展开来。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "spread out"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen044.png",
    "sha256": "2d6979715f86fb8246332ddf746d48fbfe6aec3e7284090bed34bb1bbc18043c",
    "k": 43,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They raise their hands high.",
    "zh": "他们举手也举得很高。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "raise"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen045.png",
    "sha256": "37a005b1e9e4752c54e71a18bd4ee60679c101272276ece046896a5f084fdf11",
    "k": 44,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You have other people who are virtually collapsing when they come in, as soon as they, I mean other people come in.",
    "zh": "另一些人进来时，身体却几乎是蜷缩着的；当他们——我是说，那些人——走进教室时，就是这样。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "collapse"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen046.png",
    "sha256": "2f4622a012c1bedba73951d4377d022adc4761560ea38b18073476022b95662d",
    "k": 45,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "You see it, you see it on their faces and their bodies and they sit with their chairs and they make themselves tiny.",
    "zh": "你能从他们的表情和身体姿态看出来；他们坐在椅子上，尽量让自己显得很小。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "tiny"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen047.png",
    "sha256": "7b60771e4ef0feb855b93270e290435556823b3aa2dd633928740dba3f0316a1",
    "k": 46,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And they will not fully stretch their arms when they raise their hands.",
    "zh": "而且举手时，他们也不会完全伸直手臂。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stretch"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen048.png",
    "sha256": "8451143d4d1d63862807cf86082ea57cb8422fdc4122788dd8610a7853cdc055",
    "k": 47,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I also notice another interesting thing about this.",
    "zh": "我还注意到了另一个有趣的现象。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "notice"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen049.png",
    "sha256": "98f86d311522f2d38ea8b118d91de1ddc0621e3b0ba0ec9b0c250a95a2e7cfe7",
    "k": 48,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "It seems women are much more likely to do this kind of thing than men.",
    "zh": "女性似乎比男性更容易表现出这种姿态。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "more likely to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen050.png",
    "sha256": "77210f962968a29a03161b9e521a3c992615b2a03931c93a002a3b4d127c6f00",
    "k": 49,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I mean women are more likely to make themselves small.",
    "zh": "也就是说，女性更容易让自己显得弱小。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "make oneself small"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen051.png",
    "sha256": "69ac3180c7d2d7b81128db3941ee4ad12a2c8cbe2c16992565f49b7affda8f6b",
    "k": 50,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Women feel chronically less powerful than men.",
    "zh": "女性长期以来感受到的力量往往少于男性。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "chronically"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen052.png",
    "sha256": "b170cf0e4f4bdfa8b5a679ed91fe9153271b634f39435ee3b5354307d0250ee8",
    "k": 51,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, this is not surprising.",
    "zh": "因此，这并不让人惊讶。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "surprising"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen053.png",
    "sha256": "34d41b9bb34a95c6e5176c5ce0096d7006b8d9d9236c32600a6827d83e55664a",
    "k": 52,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "The second question concerns our minds.",
    "zh": "第二个问题涉及我们的心理。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "concern"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen054.png",
    "sha256": "b5749b7c44392506dfe5cb4fd05754b9eec2637d15b2cc630944e5417234ab2c",
    "k": 53,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We know that our minds change our bodies, but is it also true that our bodies change our minds?",
    "zh": "我们知道，心理会改变身体；但身体也会改变心理，这同样成立吗？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mind"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen055.png",
    "sha256": "eb3970f655ad332e10a7a71c128da38dc76de37817b1c90b4e7fd0d916016639",
    "k": 54,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And when I say minds in the case of the powerful, what do I mean?",
    "zh": "谈到强势者的“心理”时，我指的是什么呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "in the case of"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen056.png",
    "sha256": "36f47a662e6da6ea93b0c45cd3d955aadd8b214596842ac2528354229e021b22",
    "k": 55,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I am talking about thoughts and feelings and the sorts of physiological things that make up our thoughts and feelings, and in my case, that’s hormones.",
    "zh": "我说的是思想、感受，以及构成这些思想和感受的各种生理因素；在我的研究中，具体就是激素。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "physiological"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen057.png",
    "sha256": "1c8f838a85989431ec077428cac41329f4660609da5e66041e5a151b16f2d275",
    "k": 56,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I look at hormones.",
    "zh": "我研究激素。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "hormone"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen058.png",
    "sha256": "f9bc3b9ec01e00700cec7d3dd61103358883e41043b7eeb01108c794b5ecffab",
    "k": 57,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, what do the minds of the powerful versus the powerless look like?",
    "zh": "那么，强势者和弱势者的心理分别是什么样的呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "versus"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen059.png",
    "sha256": "91eef14c0d748510b6a9fc9d832a8218a6fa028253b76ad8702dbaeb271b5a89",
    "k": 58,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Powerful people tend to be not surprisingly more assertive and more confident, more optimistic.",
    "zh": "不出所料，强势者往往更果断、更自信，也更乐观。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "assertive"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen060.png",
    "sha256": "9ceef92914ea8ad29313948fe0de24b2b46eeef9979829130aa4f1c82699a22c",
    "k": 59,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They actually feel that they’re going to win, even at games of chance.",
    "zh": "即使是在靠运气取胜的游戏中，他们也真的觉得自己会赢。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "game of chance"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen061.png",
    "sha256": "bea9e9fde97fe655a4cbac3865558c5297857c29ed67f69e3e989983f95411fb",
    "k": 60,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They also tend to be able to think more abstractly.",
    "zh": "他们也往往更能进行抽象思考。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "abstractly"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen062.png",
    "sha256": "6d181d6da065f17c12d221e11cd65d51b985e941b9925c729c752698dc0ebe4c",
    "k": 61,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "They take more risks.",
    "zh": "他们更愿意冒险。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "take risks"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen063.png",
    "sha256": "128f2c1c809e609e7b83b747c08b4ac4173e0a46973aa27477d834a8fe7768b6",
    "k": 62,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, there are a lot of differences between powerful and powerless people.",
    "zh": "因此，强势者与弱势者之间存在许多差异。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "difference"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen064.png",
    "sha256": "0a0a3d03c775d8e29067d777e0f96f58c48788380e45f97f758f8f32f4e5f277",
    "k": 63,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Physiologically, there are also differences on two key hormones.",
    "zh": "从生理上看，两种关键激素的水平也有所不同。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "physiologically"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen065.png",
    "sha256": "7dc57f66f49915c918cf6e5aceeaa425f58c39fad73705e38f6a2834a59317e0",
    "k": 64,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "One is dominance hormone and the other is stress hormone.",
    "zh": "一种是支配激素，另一种是压力激素。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stress hormone"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen066.png",
    "sha256": "79fb6b063af72382c90211a405869a4f7b56600159c4ed980ef3b66d6075830c",
    "k": 65,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What we find is that powerful and effective leaders have high dominance hormone and low stress hormone.",
    "zh": "我们发现，强势且高效的领导者，支配激素水平高，压力激素水平低。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "effective"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen067.png",
    "sha256": "14331c15dcebb3311bab7a041e8b0d7c20051b7ce82a6d1eda1f5d6420d84a7b",
    "k": 66,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What does that mean?",
    "zh": "这意味着什么呢？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mean"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen068.png",
    "sha256": "0f16eb2d7df761255f505885e4b7283b403ac45e9c62411973cc28529f55d076",
    "k": 67,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That means power is also about how you react to stress.",
    "zh": "这意味着，力量也体现在你如何应对压力上。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "react to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen069.png",
    "sha256": "322bc17cf9c5c6c594c64d6575027f344a9881c4db00a39f1ea62f4161c25694",
    "k": 68,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Once we did an experiment, we decided to bring people into the lab and run that little experiment.",
    "zh": "有一次，我们做了一项实验，把参与者请到实验室，开展了这个小实验。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "experiment"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen070.png",
    "sha256": "4baa07cdf1e29e23890c3b2eedc6f40e066ea31751576a45ca4a9831c9229ca1",
    "k": 69,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "These people adopted for two minutes either high power poses or low power poses.",
    "zh": "这些人分别保持强势姿势或弱势姿势两分钟。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "pose"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen071.png",
    "sha256": "00d7cb0bb6c4e5701c7f641622d74a410799cee69213af949ae1645a2b60dad0",
    "k": 70,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "We, for two minutes, say “You need to do this or this”.",
    "zh": "在这两分钟里，我们告诉他们：“你需要这样做，或者那样做。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "need to"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen072.png",
    "sha256": "e3e0bf7caa517645e46bab79af6810f0242b8fdea0271a3f438e6c86c467caf8",
    "k": 71,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And we also want them to be feeling power.",
    "zh": "我们也希望他们能切实感受到力量。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "power"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen073.png",
    "sha256": "704c9be6413216f31b7e3ea1c0d3e4e4cc3fdd5dc611095af876b29828f5cf36",
    "k": 72,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So after two minutes we will ask them “How powerful do you feel?” on a series of items and then we give them an opportunity to gamble.",
    "zh": "两分钟后，我们通过一组题目询问他们：“你感觉自己有多强大？”随后给他们一个参与赌博的机会。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "gamble"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen074.png",
    "sha256": "79349e41e97a1b68bdbb6ba480c0a0a3e2386e4883dba865f74620f658b218ec",
    "k": 73,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Before and after the experiment we take their samples of saliva for a hormone test.",
    "zh": "实验前后，我们采集他们的唾液样本，检测激素水平。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "saliva"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen075.png",
    "sha256": "553bde3c384a23942796cb263526d73e5dc80cfa04555a7a5a83b522f56cae5d",
    "k": 74,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "That’s the whole experiment.",
    "zh": "整个实验就是这样。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "whole"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen076.png",
    "sha256": "ce34475c9b753046f7f79149c6c36b849018e0aff3c3f5f42604d04fe7e3a8ce",
    "k": 75,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And this is what we have found: risk tolerance which is gambling.",
    "zh": "以下是我们的发现：首先是风险承受度，也就是参与赌博的意愿。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "risk tolerance"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen077.png",
    "sha256": "cf5fb6ab397867967a41d0213cee4b7e96969e193979d3a7b572f775a8ccd9f9",
    "k": 76,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "What we find is that when you’re in the higher power pose condition, 86% of you will gamble.",
    "zh": "我们发现，保持强势姿势时，有86%的人会选择参与赌博。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "condition"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen078.png",
    "sha256": "e7933d388871aceb77af12a1d1d3691e0baece8f98547ff4fb8cf25a60636c7f",
    "k": 77,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "When you’re in the low power pose condition, it’s down to only 60%, and that’s a pretty significant difference.",
    "zh": "而保持弱势姿势时，这一比例降到了仅60%，这个差异相当显著。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "significant"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen079.png",
    "sha256": "2b4b2cf5230046ae3cc8e409ff258f07461e0cf75c1b49c49e02beebc841fb30",
    "k": 78,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Here’s what we find on dominance hormone: from their baseline when they come in, ",
    "zh": "在支配激素方面，我们发现：与进入实验室时的基线水平相比，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "baseline"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen080.png",
    "sha256": "15924abfbc9eabea6a41c1100294db40970221ef11205188aa0c66f5807c7203",
    "k": 78,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "high power people experience about a 20% increase and low power people experience about a 10% decrease.",
    "zh": "强势姿势组大约上升了20%，弱势姿势组则大约下降了10%。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "increase"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen081.png",
    "sha256": "fd2dfc2028fc83566b03297a299c2828fc489be8cc84776715cc0830790d0b98",
    "k": 79,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So again, two minutes and you get these changes.",
    "zh": "所以，再强调一次，只用两分钟就能产生这些变化。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "change"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen082.png",
    "sha256": "5a5236ae9955c86487b2fcbfed281c1b8d1483c2c090838a3e233bbae647564e",
    "k": 80,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Concerning stress hormone high power people experience about a 25% decrease and the low power people experience about a 15% increase.",
    "zh": "至于压力激素，强势姿势组的水平大约下降了25%，弱势姿势组则大约上升了15%。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "decrease"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen083.png",
    "sha256": "9c683ca1770aaf24367ef7c43da2a357cf74ed51b55e1a0d48bb6d18d841a2d6",
    "k": 81,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Once again, two minutes led to these hormonal changes that configure your brain to basically be either assertive, confident or really stress-reactive.",
    "zh": "同样，只用两分钟就产生了这些激素变化，使大脑进入果断、自信，或者对压力高度敏感的状态。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "stress-reactive"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen084.png",
    "sha256": "4dd7f8c7980464e3d00aea9689a2ab42f7273045c41b37d825981b4bd17d4012",
    "k": 82,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "And you know feeling sort of shut down and we’ve all had that feeling, right?",
    "zh": "你知道，就是那种有些封闭、退缩的感觉；我们都曾有过，对吧？",
    "vocabulary": [
      "shut down"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen085.png",
    "sha256": "26ab26cca19dd697cb6133423019fb46f6965806ace12cb4a84e20e4a9abc681",
    "k": 83,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, it seems that our non-verbals do govern how we think and feel about ourselves.",
    "zh": "所以，非语言行为似乎确实会影响我们如何看待自己，以及对自己的感受。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "govern"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen086.png",
    "sha256": "64f43e4590cb92c7903416276bc672040f26eeb38b0ceec23deed58cdced2fd5",
    "k": 84,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Also, our bodies change our minds.",
    "zh": "而且，身体会改变心理。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mind"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen087.png",
    "sha256": "92670cb8a7aa1710128a581f761ea941af0afe7e4a6e0c5cfec40a7813a17be9",
    "k": 85,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, power-posing for a few minutes really changes your life in meaningful ways.",
    "zh": "因此，做几分钟强势姿势，的确能够以有意义的方式改变生活。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "meaningful"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen088.png",
    "sha256": "3dddf0a41a28f99bb43a8c6fe4972d2737c67a61da09241442d2070e488f4336",
    "k": 86,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "When I tell people about this that our bodies change our minds, and our minds can change our behavior, ",
    "zh": "当我告诉人们，身体能改变心理，心理能改变行为，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "mind"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen089.png",
    "sha256": "37d656adee4dcbcf823ff108607dfc40524fbbdeaa6570ebfcd0eb48c7342a3b",
    "k": 86,
    "part": 2,
    "parts": 2,
    "role": null,
    "en": "and our behavior can change our outcomes, they say to me “I don’t believe that. It feels fake, right?”",
    "zh": "行为又能改变结果时，他们会说：“我不相信。这感觉很假，对吧？”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "outcome"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen090.png",
    "sha256": "a3fe97bec376f6da782949c2f75194204cbd41882e868cb6da7891e0a22f4282",
    "k": 87,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "So, I said, “fake it till you make it”.",
    "zh": "所以我说：“先做出那个样子，直到真正做到。”",
    "vocabulary": [
      "fake it till you make it"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen091.png",
    "sha256": "d9b31d82812bdf337973712bc0835ea71ae9081ab4a2bfeddb6f76a8249d49b9",
    "k": 88,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "I’m going to leave you with this.",
    "zh": "最后，我想留给大家这样一个建议。",
    "vocabulary": [
      "leave someone with something"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen092.png",
    "sha256": "55408dd8f62452ab20452e345b97e19e5a1552e5b4a4e8c7135528e95dacf20f",
    "k": 89,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "Before you go into the next stressful evaluative situation, for example, a job interview.",
    "zh": "在下一次进入需要接受评价、又充满压力的场合之前，比如参加求职面试之前，",
    "vocabulary": [
      "evaluative"
    ]
  },
  {
    "file": "screen093.png",
    "sha256": "c834a3ab7e91210a5226e79c1a148e312610ba328d05b0bc0df77952411d7c86",
    "k": 90,
    "part": 1,
    "parts": 1,
    "role": null,
    "en": "For two minutes, try doing this, in the elevator or at your desk behind closed doors, and say to yourself “That’s what I want to do”.",
    "zh": "试着花两分钟做这些动作，可以在电梯里，也可以在关上门的办公桌前；对自己说：“这就是我要做的。”",
    "vocabulary": [
